  "result": "Perfect! All 259 tests pass. I've successfully added the CSV export functionality.\n\n**exportCsv(invoices)** - New function in src/export.js:\n- **Returns** a CSV string with header and one line per invoice\n- **Header**: number,customer,issueDate,dueDate,status,subtotal,discount,vat,total,due\n- **Fields**:\n  - `number`: invoice number (empty for draft)\n  - `customer`: customer name (looked up from customerId)\n  - `issueDate`, `dueDate`: dates (empty dueDate for draft if none)\n  - `status`: draft/issued/partially_paid/paid\n  - Amounts: euros with 2 decimals, no currency sign, no thousands separator (e.g., 1234.50)\n- **CSV escaping**: Double quotes around fields with commas/quotes/newlines, internal quotes doubled\n- **Line endings**: Each line ends with \\n\n\n**Tests added** - 13 new tests covering:\n- Empty array (header only)\n- Single issued invoice\n- Amount formatting (euros with 2 decimals)\n- Draft invoices (no number)\n- Customer names with commas\n- Customer names with quotes (proper escaping)\n- Multiple invoices\n- Partially paid invoices\n- Paid invoices (0.00 due)\n- Voucher-applied invoices\n- Line discounts\n- Customer not found\n- Zero amounts\n\nThe export correctly handles all invoice states and produces valid CSV that can be imported into accounting software.",
